{#- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    THEME TAPE (#theme-tape / .tt-*) — us_stocks, mode == 'stocks'.
    主题热度 — 热门主题与本榜的对应关系。

    WHAT THIS IS.
    Charter: research/PROPHET_US_TREND_INTELLIGENCE_MASTERPLAN_BY_FABLE.md §W2.
    Data:    engine/theme_tape.py (the whole join is Python; this file only lays out
             a finished dict — no membership logic, no counting, no sorting here).

    It closes ONE gap, and the operator named it: the rotation engine knows Software
    is the hottest theme in the market, the member map exists, and the board said
    nothing about either. This panel is the standing fix for detection-without-
    narration (Mag-7 silence postmortem, 2026-08-03).

    IT IS AN ACCOUNTING, NOT A LEADERBOARD — that distinction is the whole design.
    Heat in, names out, remainder explained. Its value does not rest on the heat read
    being predictive (it is not proven — see the null below); it rests on what the
    board is DOING with those names, which is an observable fact. That is why a hot
    theme with zero board names still gets a line, and the line says so. A panel that
    only spoke when it had a pick would reproduce the silence it exists to fix.

    DESIGN NOTE — why the ladder is a fixed grid and why only one figure is coloured.
    The five state columns hold fixed positions under one persistent header, so the
    eye can scan DOWN a column ("does anything have a live name today?") as easily as
    across a row. A zero is printed as an en-dash in its slot rather than collapsed:
    printed absence is the point of the panel, and a missing cell would break the
    column scan. Colour appears on exactly ONE glyph — the `live` count, and only when
    it is non-zero — via --ink-up, which flips under 红涨绿跌 at paint. Colouring all
    five columns would re-encode a cohort STATE into signal furniture, which is
    precisely the construction the 2026-07-23 ruling removed; the states are carried
    by POSITION and by the header's words, never by hue.
    The quiet remainder is written as a fraction ("54/60"), never a bare count: the
    denominator is what makes it information instead of decoration (Law 3).
    Zero animation, zero transition — so no reduced-motion block is required here.
    Add one and you must gate it, naming the pseudos.

    TIERS (docs/DESIGN_DOCTRINE.md):
      1 GLANCE  eyebrow · one grid line + one stance line per theme · one footer
      2 HOVER   the panel `?` carries the method AND the Law-5 null receipt;
                per-theme receipts (relative strength, score) ride data-tip-*
      3 STUDY   the expanded member list, and subsector_rotation.html for the
                full 41-theme table
    Every stance sentence is chosen MECHANICALLY from the counts by
    engine/theme_tape.py `_stance_for` — no free-form text reaches this file, and the
    verbs come from the doctrine's sanctioned stance vocabulary.
    No translated text ever enters a title= attribute (CI-guarded); every tip is a
    hand-written data-tip-* attribute, never piped through t()/help(), which emit
    spans and would break attribute quoting.

    TIER PREVIEW. The COUNTS are free — they are aggregate and they are the panel's
    argument. The member NAMES are the product, so `.tt-names` collapses to a count
    for anonymous and Free visitors through the same reversible data-mx-old-html
    stash templates/tier_preview.js already uses for the themes-in-favour strip.

    CONTEXT IT READS (fail-open; absence renders exactly like a quiet tape):
      theme_tape  {as_of, board_as_of, rank_of, rows[], measuring, n_days}
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -#}

{%- macro tt_t(en, zh='') -%}
<span class="l-en">{{ en }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ zh if zh else en }}</span>
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- English ordinal for the theme's place in the rotation table. Capped at the
    handful the panel can ever show; anything else degrades to "Nth", which is
    still readable and never wrong. -#}
{%- macro tt_ord(n) -%}
{%- set _o = {1:'1st', 2:'2nd', 3:'3rd', 4:'4th', 5:'5th', 6:'6th', 7:'7th', 8:'8th'} -%}
{{ _o.get(n, (n|string) ~ 'th') }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- set _tt = theme_tape if (theme_tape is defined and theme_tape is mapping) else none -%}
{%- set _tt_rows = (_tt.get('rows') or []) if _tt else [] -%}

{#- Honest-null gate (DO_NOT_REBUILD row 151 — no forced ranking in a dead tape).
    engine/theme_tape.py returns None when nothing clears the constructive floor, so
    reaching this guard with no rows means the tape is dead and the panel emits
    NOTHING AT ALL — no shell, no <style>, no empty box. -#}
{%- if _tt_rows -%}
{%- set _tt_cols = [
      ('live',       'live',       '可操作'),
      ('setting_up', 'setting up', '形成中'),
      ('ran',        'ran',        '已启动'),
      ('leading',    'leading',    '领跑'),
      ('watching',   'watching',   '观察中')
    ] -%}
  <style id="theme-tape-css">
  /* ── THEME TAPE (W2) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Every value resolves from an existing theme.css token. No new hex, theme.css
     untouched, so light / dark / zh all repaint at color-mix time with nothing to
     keep in sync. */
  body.page-stocks #theme-tape{padding:15px 18px 14px}
  body.page-stocks .tt-hd{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:6px 12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:0 0 4px}
  body.page-stocks .tt-eyebrow{margin:0;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.18em;
    text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.2}
  /* zh Hanzi read wrong under Latin display tracking — theme.css makes the same
     call for headings; the eyebrow keeps its rhythm from weight and colour. */
  html[data-lang="zh"] body.page-stocks .tt-eyebrow{letter-spacing:.06em}
  body.page-stocks .tt-asof{margin-left:auto;font-family:var(--font-mono,monospace);font-size:10.5px;
    color:var(--muted);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}
  body.page-stocks .tt-sub{font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 10px;max-width:74ch}

  /* THE LADDER GRID. One template shared by the header and every row, so the
     columns cannot drift apart. Fixed numeric widths (not max-content) are what
     make the columns a COLUMN: max-content would size per row and the figures
     would never line up. 58px clears "setting up" at 10px in both languages;
     66px clears "54/60" at 12.5px mono. */
  body.page-stocks .tt-cols,
  body.page-stocks .tt-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) repeat(5,58px) 66px;
    gap:0 6px;align-items:baseline}
  body.page-stocks .tt-cols{padding:0 0 5px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);margin:0 0 2px}
  body.page-stocks .tt-k{font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--muted);
    text-align:right;line-height:1.25}
  html[data-lang="zh"] body.page-stocks .tt-k{letter-spacing:0}
  body.page-stocks .tt-k-quiet{text-align:right}

  /* Each theme is one <details>. The summary holds BOTH glance lines, so the whole
     row is the disclosure control — a large, obvious tap target on a phone. */
  body.page-stocks .tt-i{border-bottom:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,var(--line) 55%,transparent)}
  body.page-stocks .tt-i:last-of-type{border-bottom:0}
  body.page-stocks .tt-s{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;padding:9px 0 8px}
  body.page-stocks .tt-s::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
  body.page-stocks .tt-s:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ink-link,var(--link,var(--text)));
    outline-offset:2px;border-radius:3px}
  body.page-stocks .tt-nm{font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);min-width:0}
  /* The caret is a pseudo, so it stays out of any copy a vocabulary scan reads and
     needs no translation. It rotates by being replaced, not by a transform, so
     there is nothing here for reduced-motion to gate. */
  body.page-stocks .tt-s .tt-nm::before{content:"▸";color:var(--muted);font-size:10px;
    margin-right:6px;display:inline-block;vertical-align:1px}
  body.page-stocks .tt-i[open] .tt-s .tt-nm::before{content:"▾"}
  body.page-stocks .tt-heat{display:block;font-size:11px;font-weight:400;color:var(--muted);
    margin-top:2px;padding-left:16px}
  /* THE FIGURES. Mono + tabular so the digits stack; the body face would ripple
     the column. Words never take the mono face — the header above is body-face.
     The right edge is set on the CELL, which is the grid item; setting it on the
     figure inside would align nothing, because the figure is only as wide as it
     needs to be. */
  body.page-stocks .tt-c{text-align:right;min-width:0}
  body.page-stocks .tt-v{font-family:var(--font-mono,monospace);font-size:13px;font-weight:700;
    font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--text);white-space:nowrap}
  /* The ONLY colour on the panel, and only ever on a non-zero `live` count — the
     one cell that means "there is something to do today". --ink-* is the
     text-grade form of the state palette (raw --up is fill-grade and misses the
     contrast floor as light-theme text); the var() fallback keeps a cache-stale
     theme.css rendering today's colour rather than an invalid declaration. */
  body.page-stocks .tt-v.is-live{color:var(--ink-up,var(--up))}
  /* A printed absence, at the weight of an absence. */
  body.page-stocks .tt-v.is-zero{color:var(--muted);opacity:.5;font-weight:600}
  body.page-stocks .tt-quiet{font-family:var(--font-mono,monospace);font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;
    font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap}
  body.page-stocks .tt-say{font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--text);
    padding-left:16px;margin-top:3px}
  body.page-stocks .tt-stance{font-weight:650}

  /* Tier 3 — the member list. Indented under the row it belongs to, and quiet: it
     is a reference list, not a second board. */
  body.page-stocks .tt-det{padding:2px 0 12px 16px}
  body.page-stocks .tt-g{display:grid;grid-template-columns:74px minmax(0,1fr);gap:0 10px;
    align-items:baseline;padding:3px 0}
  body.page-stocks .tt-gk{font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted);text-align:right;
    line-height:1.5}
  body.page-stocks .tt-names{font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--text);min-width:0;
    overflow-wrap:anywhere}
  /* NOT nowrap. A ticker must never break, but a name carries its reason inside this
     span ("AMZN · already extended — watch, don't chase"), and holding the PAIR on
     one line made an opened row 516px wide inside a 390px phone — the page itself
     scrolled sideways, which this panel is not allowed to cause. The unbreakable
     unit is the symbol; the sentence after it wraps like any other sentence. */
  body.page-stocks .tt-n{white-space:normal}
  /* Two separators, one glyph, deliberately different widths. A mixed group reads
     "AMZN · already extended — watch, don't chase · WMT · entry window has passed":
     with equal spacing the eye cannot tell which middot ends a name and which
     introduces its reason. The name boundary gets nearly twice the air, so the
     rhythm itself groups each ticker with the reason that belongs to it. */
  body.page-stocks .tt-n + .tt-n::before{content:"·";color:var(--muted);padding:0 9px;opacity:.6}
  body.page-stocks .tt-sym{font-family:var(--font-mono,monospace);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.02em;
    white-space:nowrap}
  /* The reason hangs off the name behind a middot, not a dash: the reason text has
     its own em-dash inside it ("already extended — watch, don't chase"), and two
     dashes in one phrase read as one muddled clause. A middot needs no translation,
     so both languages take the same rule. It is a pseudo, not a text node, so it
     keeps its spacing however the markup wraps and stays out of any copy a
     vocabulary scan reads. */
  body.page-stocks .tt-why{color:var(--muted);font-size:11px}
  body.page-stocks .tt-why::before{content:"·";padding:0 5px 0 4px;opacity:.5}
  body.page-stocks .tt-more{color:var(--muted);font-weight:600}

  body.page-stocks .tt-rule{border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:8px 0 10px}
  body.page-stocks .tt-foot{margin:0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--muted);max-width:74ch}
  body.page-stocks .tt-foot a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px}

  @media (max-width:900px){
    body.page-stocks #theme-tape .tt-asof{margin-left:0}
  }
  /* ── phones (≤680px, the board's own mobile break, #4344) ───────────────────
     The six-column alignment is a desktop luxury: it exists so a reader can scan
     one column across five themes. On a phone you read one theme at a time, so
     the ladder becomes a flowing line of "N label" pairs and the header row —
     whose only job was to label those columns — is dropped. Each cell then shows
     its own label, and a ZERO cell is removed entirely: a printed en-dash is
     honest inside a column, but "0 watching" in a sentence is just noise.
     Nothing here scrolls sideways; the row wraps. */
  @media (max-width:680px){
    body.page-stocks #theme-tape{padding:13px 14px}
    body.page-stocks .tt-cols{display:none}
    body.page-stocks .tt-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:2px 10px}
    body.page-stocks .tt-nm{flex:1 0 100%}
    body.page-stocks .tt-c{display:inline-flex;align-items:baseline;gap:4px}
    body.page-stocks .tt-c.is-zero-cell{display:none}
    body.page-stocks .tt-c .tt-ik{font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);font-style:normal}
    body.page-stocks .tt-v,body.page-stocks .tt-quiet{text-align:left;font-size:12.5px}
    body.page-stocks .tt-g{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:0}
    body.page-stocks .tt-gk{text-align:left}
  }
  /* The per-cell label is redundant wherever the header row is visible. */
  @media (min-width:681px){
    body.page-stocks .tt-c .tt-ik{display:none}
  }
  </style>
  <div class="panel span12" id="theme-tape">
    <div class="tt-hd">
      <h2 class="tt-eyebrow">{{ tt_t('Theme heat', '主题热度') }}</h2>
      {#- Tier-2: the method AND the Law-5 receipt live here, together, so the panel
          carries exactly one `?` and one footnote. -#}
      <span class="help">?<span class="tip tip-wide"><span class="l-en">The market's fastest-accelerating themes, each one reconciled against this board: every member of the theme is placed in exactly one column, so the row adds up to the theme's whole membership. A name is counted at its most actionable state, and a name can sit in more than one theme. Scorecard: the rotation read grades its own calls nightly against realized member-equal-weight returns relative to SPY; after {{ _tt.get('n_days') or 0 }} graded days no horizon has cleared its significance bar, so treat the ordering as a place to look, not as an edge. Nothing on this panel ranks, gates or sizes anything — the board below is unchanged by it.</span><span class="l-zh">当前加速最快的主题，并逐一对照本榜：主题的每一只成分股都被归入且仅归入一列，因此整行相加等于该主题的全部成分股。同一只股票按其最可操作的状态计入，且可能同时属于多个主题。记分卡：轮动研判每晚以成分股等权、相对 SPY 的实际收益为自身研判评分；已评分 {{ _tt.get('n_days') or 0 }} 天，尚无周期通过显著性检验，因此这一排序只用于确定观察方向，不构成优势证据。本面板不参与任何排名、筛选或仓位决定，下方看板不受其影响。</span></span></span>
      {%- if _tt.get('as_of') %}
      <span class="tt-asof">{{ tt_t('as of ' ~ _tt.as_of, '截至 ' ~ _tt.as_of) }}</span>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    <p class="tt-sub">{{ tt_t('The market’s hottest themes, and what this board is doing with their names.',
                              '当前最热的主题，以及本榜对其成分股的处理。') }}</p>

    {#- The header row is the ONLY label source where it is visible; each cell also
        carries its own label for the phone layout, and exactly one of the two is in
        the accessibility tree at any breakpoint (the other is display:none). -#}
    <div class="tt-cols">
      <span></span>
      {%- for _k, _en, _zh in _tt_cols %}<span class="tt-k">{{ tt_t(_en, _zh) }}</span>{% endfor %}
      <span class="tt-k tt-k-quiet">{{ tt_t('quiet', '未触发') }}</span>
    </div>

    {%- for _r in _tt_rows %}
    {%- set _c = _r.get('counts') or {} %}
    <details class="tt-i">
      <summary class="tt-s">
        <div class="tt-row"
             data-tip-en="{{ _r.name }} — {{ tt_ord(_r.rank) }} of {{ _tt.get('rank_of') or 0 }} themes by acceleration{% if _r.get('rs_1m') is not none %}, {{ '%+.1f'|format(_r.rs_1m|float)|replace('-', '−') }}% against the market over the past month{% endif %}{% if _r.get('rs_1w') is not none %} and {{ '%+.1f'|format(_r.rs_1w|float)|replace('-', '−') }}% over the past week{% endif %}. {{ _r.n_on_board }} of its {{ _r.n_members }} members are on this board. Display context only — this changes no ranking below."
             data-tip-zh="{{ _r.name }} — 按加速度在 {{ _tt.get('rank_of') or 0 }} 个主题中排名第 {{ _r.rank }}{% if _r.get('rs_1m') is not none %}，过去一个月相对大盘 {{ '%+.1f'|format(_r.rs_1m|float)|replace('-', '−') }}%{% endif %}{% if _r.get('rs_1w') is not none %}，过去一周 {{ '%+.1f'|format(_r.rs_1w|float)|replace('-', '−') }}%{% endif %}。其 {{ _r.n_members }} 只成分股中有 {{ _r.n_on_board }} 只在本榜上。仅为展示参考，不改变下方任何排序。">
          <span class="tt-nm">{{ tt_t(_r.name, _r.name_zh) }}
            <span class="tt-heat">{{ tt_t(tt_ord(_r.rank) ~ ' of ' ~ (_tt.get('rank_of') or 0),
                                          '第 ' ~ _r.rank ~ ' 名，共 ' ~ (_tt.get('rank_of') or 0)) }}{% if _r.get('heat_en') %} · {{ tt_t(_r.heat_en, _r.heat_zh) }}{% endif %}</span>
          </span>
          {%- for _k, _en, _zh in _tt_cols %}
          {%- set _n = _c.get(_k) or 0 %}
          <span class="tt-c{% if not _n %} is-zero-cell{% endif %}"><b class="tt-v{% if _n and _k == 'live' %} is-live{% endif %}{% if not _n %} is-zero{% endif %}">{% if _n %}{{ _n }}{% else %}–{% endif %}</b><i class="tt-ik">{{ tt_t(_en, _zh) }}</i></span>
          {%- endfor %}
          <span class="tt-c"><b class="tt-quiet">{{ _c.get('quiet') or 0 }}/{{ _r.n_members }}</b><i class="tt-ik">{{ tt_t('quiet', '未触发') }}</i></span>
        </div>
        {#- Law 1 — the stance. Selected mechanically from the counts above by
            engine/theme_tape.py; this file only prints the pair it was handed. -#}
        <div class="tt-say"><span class="tt-stance">{{ tt_t(_r.say_en, _r.say_zh) }}</span></div>
      </summary>
      <div class="tt-det">
        {%- for _k, _en, _zh in _tt_cols %}
        {%- set _mem = (_r.get('members') or {}).get(_k) or [] %}
        {%- set _shared = (_r.get('shared_why') or {}).get(_k) %}
        {%- if _mem %}
        <div class="tt-g">
          <span class="tt-gk">{{ tt_t(_en, _zh) }}</span>
          <span class="tt-names">{% for _m in _mem %}<span class="tt-n"><span class="tt-sym">{{ _m.t }}</span>{% if _m.get('why_en') %}<span class="tt-why">{{ tt_t(_m.why_en, _m.why_zh) }}</span>{% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}{% if _shared %}<span class="tt-why">{{ tt_t(_shared[0], _shared[1]) }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
        {#- The remainder. ONE shared reason, stated once, never invented per name:
            the board has no row for these, so there is no per-name verdict to
            report — saying otherwise would be a fabricated rejection. -#}
        {%- if _r.get('quiet_sample') %}
        <div class="tt-g">
          <span class="tt-gk">{{ tt_t('quiet', '未触发') }}</span>
          <span class="tt-names">{% for _q in _r.quiet_sample %}<span class="tt-n"><span class="tt-sym">{{ _q }}</span></span>{% endfor %}{% if _r.get('quiet_more') %}<span class="tt-n tt-more">+{{ _r.quiet_more }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="tt-why">{{ tt_t('no fresh entry trigger today', '今日无新入场触发') }}</span></span>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </details>
    {%- endfor %}

    {#- ONE footnote, merged (Law 4). It carries the plain-word null first, because
        that is the thing a reader most needs to know before acting on an ordering,
        then the overlap fact — which exists because a mega-cap really does sit in
        five of today's themes, and a reader who sees the same ticker on five lines
        deserves to know why rather than to suspect a bug. -#}
    <hr class="tt-rule">
    <p class="tt-foot">
      <span class="l-en">{% if _tt.get('measuring') %}Theme heat is a read still being measured — it points you at where to look, not at what to buy; the picks below are unchanged by it. {% endif %}A large company can sit in several themes, so the same ticker may appear on more than one line. <a href="subsector_rotation.html">All {{ _tt.get('rank_of') or 0 }} themes →</a></span>
      <span class="l-zh">{% if _tt.get('measuring') %}主题热度仍在检验中 — 它指出值得关注的方向，而非买入对象；下方选股不受其影响。{% endif %}大型公司可能同时属于多个主题，因此同一代码可能出现在多行中。<a href="subsector_rotation.html">查看全部 {{ _tt.get('rank_of') or 0 }} 个主题 →</a></span>
    </p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
